 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Channel Performance:** A 2-channel volume texture is usually much slower on multiple vendors' GPUs and should be avoided [S2, unofficial].
-- **Resolution Mismatch:** Linear sampling across normalized coordinates allows filtering across resolution boundaries, but may blur high-frequency details if the unified texture is significantly larger than a source texture [S1, unofficial].
-- **Precision Loss:** Storing floating-point values in 8-bit channels causes quantization [S3].
-- **Channel Limit:** Standard RGBA provides only 4 channels [S1, unofficial]. Separate textures are required for more than 4 channels or different storage types/precisions [S2, unofficial].
